:"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":0.150622,"donor_lfcse":0.478216,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":6.96344e-07,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000170820","module":"turquoise","kme":0.147783,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000170820","entrez_id":["2492"],"uniprot":["P23945"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene belongs to family 1 of G-protein coupled receptors. It is the receptor for follicle stimulating hormone and functions in gonad development. Mutations in this gene cause ovarian dysgenesis type 1, and also ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Mar 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P23945","text":"G protein-coupled receptor for follitropin, the follicle-stimulating hormone (PubMed:11847099, PubMed:24058690, PubMed:24692546). Mediates FSH signaling through cAMP/protein kinase A (PKA) and phosphatidylinositol-3 kinase (PI3K)/protein kinase B (AKT) pathways to regulate ovarian follicular development and steroidogenesis (PubMed:24058690). Has diverse extragonadal functions: signals via a GNAI2-coupled FSHR on osteoclasts and their precursors, resulting in activation of MEK/ERK, NF-kappa-B, and AKT pathways and thus increases osteoclastogenesis and bone resorption (By similarity). Regulates glucose-stimulated insulin secretion in pancreatic beta-cells in a bell curve manner, with moderate FSH levels promoting insulin secretion via Galphas/cAMP/PKA pathways while high FSH levels inhibit this effect through Galphai coupling (By similarity). In adipose tissue, inhibits thermogenesis by suppressing UCP1 expression and promotes lipogenesis via CREB/PPARgamma pathways (By similarity). Also affects hepatic cholesterol metabolism by increasing serum total and low-density-lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL-C) by inhibiting the expression of LDL receptor (LDLR) (PubMed:26583582)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}